2. **February Revolution (1917)**: This revolution, also known as the February Bourgeois Democratic Revolution, was the first of two revolutions in Russia in 1917. It began with mass protests against food rationing in Petrograd (now St. Petersburg) and lasted about eight days, involving mass demonstrations and violent clashes with police and gendarmes.
3. **October Revolution (1917)**: Also known as the Great October Socialist Revolution, this revolution was led by the Bolsheviks and Vladimir Lenin, and it was instrumental in the larger Russian Revolution of 1917. It took place with an armed insurrection in Petrograd on 7 November (25 October, O.S.) 1917.

