What is the production history of the Toyota 4Runner, including its first generation and subsequent updates?
The Toyota 4Runner was first produced in May 1984. The first generation (1984-1989) featured a compact SUV design with a fiberglass shell over a pickup truck bed. It was initially equipped with a 2.4 L 22R engine and a four-wheel-drive system that drove the front wheels through a solid front axle.

In 1985, the 2.4 L 22R-E engine was introduced, which was electronically fuel-injected and had California emissions controls.

The second generation (1990-1995) saw minor cosmetic updates, including one-piece front bumpers and modular headlamps, for the 1992 model year. This update distanced the 4Runner from the Hilux.

Note: The provided context does not mention the production history beyond the second generation, so I have only included the information available.
