Based on the provided context, the specific article in the Universal Declaration of Human Rights (UDHR) that guarantees the right to family is:

**Article 16**

The key provisions of Article 16 are:

"(1) Men and women of full age, without any limitation due to race, nationality or religion, have the right to marry and to found a family. They are entitled to equal rights as to marriage, during marriage and at its dissolution.

(2) Marriage shall be entered into only with the free and full consent of the intending spouses.

(3) The family is the natural and fundamental group unit of society and is entitled to protection by society and the State.

(4) The right to marry and to found a family is recognized, in community with one's choice, without any limitation due to race, nationality or religion.

(5) The family is entitled to protection by society and the State.

(6) The right of men and women of full age, without any limitation due to race, nationality or religion, to marry and to found a family will be recognized.

(7) The children born out of wedlock shall enjoy the same rights as natural children before the law.

(8) Parents have a prior right to choose the education and religion of their children, provided that the best interests of the child are respected."

These provisions emphasize the importance of family life, equality in marriage, and the protection of the family unit by society and the State.
